---
/**
 * The coupling-map panel (MASTER_BUILD_PLAN §5.1, handbook Table H-1): a
 * collapsible "if you change X → direct effect → knock-ons to watch" table.
 * Read the third column before committing the first.
 */
import { COUPLING_MAP } from '../lib/config';
---
<details class="coupling-panel">
  <summary>Coupling map — how every decision pulls three others (handbook Part H)</summary>
  <div class="ct-wrap">
    <table class="coupling-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>If you change…</th><th>Direct effect</th><th>Knock-ons to watch</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {COUPLING_MAP.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{r.change}</td>
            <td>{r.direct}</td>
            <td class="ko">{r.knockOns}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="ct-foot" style="padding:0 1rem 0.8rem;">
    Before any change, say it out loud: "this changes [direct], which also moves [X]
    and [Y], and I'll verify [X],[Y] with [measurement]." If you can't name the
    knock-ons, you're not ready to make the change.
  </p>
</details>
